# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [0.7.0] - 2026-01-22

### Added
- **Internationalization (i18n) Support for Admin Panel**
  - Added English translations for staff management section
    - Staff status labels (Active/Inactive) with `data-i18n` attributes
    - Edit staff form labels and fields (Full Name, Email, Phone, Position, Department, Status)
    - View staff modal labels (ID, Full Name, Email, Phone, Position, Department, Hire Date, Status)
  - Added English translations for user management section
    - View user modal labels (ID, Username, Full Name, Email, Phone, Role)
    - Edit user form labels and fields (Username, Full Name, Email, Phone, Role)
    - User role options (User, Receptionist, Administrator)
    - Action buttons (View, Edit, Delete) in users table
  - Added English translations for service requests in receptionist panel
    - Empty state message for service requests table
- **Reports Dashboard Enhancement**
  - Integrated Chart.js library for data visualization
  - Automatic report generation and display when opening Reports tab
    - Revenue report with doughnut chart showing total revenue
    - Occupancy report with bar chart showing booking status distribution
    - Booking report with pie chart showing booking status breakdown
  - Removed date range input controls - reports now automatically show last 30 days
  - Real-time statistics display below each chart
    - Revenue: Total revenue, number of payments, average per payment
    - Occupancy: Total bookings, confirmed, pending, checked-out, cancelled
    - Bookings: Detailed status breakdown with counts

### Changed
- **Reports Tab UI/UX**
  - Replaced manual report generation with automatic loading
  - Charts now display immediately when Reports tab is opened
  - Removed date picker inputs and "Generate Report" buttons
  - Added responsive chart containers with fixed height (300px)
  - Statistics displayed in styled cards below charts
- **Report Service Implementation**
  - Updated `generate_revenue_report()`, `generate_occupancy_report()`, and `generate_booking_report()` 
    to work without date parameters (uses last 30 days by default)
  - Improved data structure returned from report services for better chart rendering

### Fixed
- **Report Repository JSON Serialization**
  - Fixed `MySQLInterfaceError: Python type dict cannot be converted` error
  - Improved JSON serialization in `ReportRepository.save()` method
    - Properly converts dictionaries and lists to JSON strings before database insertion
    - Handles string, dict, list, and None values correctly
    - Uses `json.dumps()` with `ensure_ascii=False` for proper Unicode support
- **Report Service Parameter Order**
  - Fixed incorrect parameter order in `ReportService` methods
    - Removed incorrect `datetime.now().isoformat()` parameter from `save()` calls
    - Corrected parameter order: `save(report_type, data, period_start, period_end)`
- **Staff Status Display**
  - Fixed hardcoded Vietnamese text "Hoạt Động"/"Không Hoạt Động" in staff table
  - Now uses `LanguageManager.getTranslation()` for proper i18n support
  - Status displays correctly in both Vietnamese and English

### Technical Details
- Added Chart.js CDN (v4.4.0) to `admin.html`
- Created `loadReports()` function that automatically loads all reports on tab switch
- Updated `switchTab()` to call `loadReports()` when Reports tab is activated
- Chart instances are properly destroyed and recreated to prevent memory leaks
- Report data structure supports both `report.data` and direct `report` properties for backward compatibility

## [0.6.0] - 2026-01-18

### Changed
- **UI Structure Reorganization**: Reorganized frontend files into role-based folders for better maintainability
  - Created `auth/` folder for authentication pages (login.html, register.html)
  - Created `public/` folder for public pages (rooms.html, room-detail.html, contact.html)
  - Created `user/` folder for user features (dashboard.html, my-bookings.html, payment.html, wallet.html)
  - Created `admin/` folder for admin & staff panels (admin.html, admin-messages.html, receptionist.html)
  - Kept `index.html` at root level as landing page
- **Path Management**: Updated all HTML files with correct relative paths
  - CSS/JS paths updated: `css/` → `../css/` for subfolders
  - Navigation links updated to reflect new folder structure
  - Image paths updated: `images/` → `../images/` for subfolders
- **Authentication Redirects**: Enhanced `AuthManager` with automatic path calculation
  - Added `_getPathToRoot()` helper function to detect current location
  - `getRedirectUrl()` now automatically calculates correct paths based on current folder
  - `logout()`, `requireAuth()`, and `blockAdminAccess()` updated to use dynamic paths
  - Prevents path errors when navigating between different folder levels

### Fixed
- Fixed incorrect redirect paths in `payment.html` and `my-bookings.html`
  - Updated `rooms.html` redirects to `../public/rooms.html`
- Fixed navigation links in `contact.html` pointing to wrong folders
  - Updated dashboard, my-bookings, wallet links to correct `../user/` paths
- Fixed `getRedirectUrl()` returning incorrect paths when called from subfolders
  - Now correctly handles paths from `auth/`, `user/`, `admin/`, and `public/` folders
- Fixed logout redirect causing "Cannot GET /SRC/index.html" error
  - Logout now correctly redirects to `index.html` regardless of current folder

### Documentation
- Updated README.md Project Structure section to reflect new UI organization
  - Added detailed folder structure showing role-based organization
  - Documented purpose of each folder (auth, public, user, admin)

## [0.5.0] - 2026-01-11

### Added
- User Management tab in Admin Panel (`admin.html`)
  - View all users with role-based sorting (administrator > receptionist > user)
  - View user details modal
  - Edit user information (full name, phone, email, role)
  - Delete user functionality
  - Search and filter users by name
- Service Request Management tab in Receptionist Panel (`receptionist.html`)
  - View all service requests with booking and service details
  - Update service request status (pending, in_progress, completed, cancelled)
  - Add notes when updating service request status
  - Filter service requests by status
  - Display service request information including booking ID, service name, quantity, and total price
- Service deletion protection
  - Prevents deletion of services that have associated service requests
  - Shows user-friendly error message with count of linked service requests

### Changed
- Admin Panel: Removed receptionist account creation when adding new staff
  - Simplified staff management workflow
  - Single main receptionist account is sufficient for system operations
- Room listing display: Limited to maximum 2 rooms per row on larger screens
  - Improved visual layout and readability
  - Better use of screen space
- API error handling improvements (`api.js`)
  - Enhanced network error detection and reporting
  - Better handling of non-JSON responses
  - More detailed error messages for troubleshooting server connectivity issues
  - Checks `content-type` header before parsing JSON responses
- Service request status update: Only sends `notes` parameter if it has a value
  - Prevents sending `null` values in API requests

### Fixed
- Fixed `UnboundLocalError` in `service_controller.py`
  - Resolved variable name conflict between Flask's `request` object and local variable
  - Changed local variable name from `request` to `service_request` to avoid conflicts
- Fixed service request status update connectivity errors
  - Improved error handling provides clearer diagnostic information
  - Better user feedback when server connection fails

## [0.4.0] - 2026-01-10

### Added
- Service request system for ordering additional services during stay
  - New `service_requests` table in database
  - `ServiceRequest` model and `ServiceRequestRepository` for persistence
  - Service costs integration into checkout process
- Checkout summary endpoint (`GET /api/checkouts/summary/<booking_id>`) displaying booking price and service costs
- Multiple bookings display in check-in/check-out workflow
  - When searching by guest name, all eligible bookings are shown for selection
  - Improved UX for handling guests with multiple room bookings
- Cash payment option in payment page alongside wallet payment
- Cancel booking modal with reason input and deposit loss warning
- CSS extraction for better maintainability
  - Extracted inline CSS from `contact.html` to `css/contact.css`
  - Extracted inline CSS from `my-bookings.html` to `css/my-bookings.css`
- Dashboard improvements for checked-in users
  - "Phòng Đang Sử Dụng" section displaying only checked-in rooms
  - Service ordering functionality directly from dashboard
  - View ordered services modal with total price updates
- Automatic room assignment during check-in (no manual room ID input required)
- Room status auto-update: rooms are set to 'reserved' when booking is created, 'available' when cancelled
- Smooth scroll navigation from homepage menu to sections (GIỚI THIỆU, PHÒNG)
- Room listing UI redesign with modern card layout matching provided design

### Changed
- Booking flow refactored: redirects to `payment.html` before creating booking
  - Booking details saved as draft in `localStorage`
  - Actual booking creation happens after payment confirmation or cash selection
- Check-in process: automatic room assignment based on room type
  - Removed requirement for manual room ID input
  - System automatically selects available room matching booking's room type
- Check-out process: displays service costs and calculates total amount
  - Shows breakdown of booking price, service costs, and total payment
  - Service requests are included in checkout calculation
- Dashboard: removed booking statistics, focused on current stay management
  - Only displays checked-in rooms for active users
  - Total price dynamically updates when services are ordered
- Receptionist panel: enhanced check-in/check-out search
  - Displays all matching bookings when multiple rooms are booked
  - Improved selection interface for choosing which booking to process
- Room detail page: added validation to prevent booking unavailable rooms
  - Disables booking button for 'occupied', 'maintenance', or 'reserved' rooms
- Payment service: removed automatic booking confirmation after payment
  - Bookings remain 'pending' until manually confirmed by receptionist
- Booking service: improved error handling with rollback on payment failure
  - Booking is cancelled if payment processing fails
  - Room status is reverted if booking creation fails

### Fixed
- Fixed booking status incorrectly showing 'confirmed' immediately after creation
  - Bookings now correctly remain 'pending' until receptionist confirmation
- Fixed room status not updating to 'reserved' when booking is created
  - Rooms are now properly reserved upon successful booking
- Fixed wallet balance validation: users cannot proceed with booking if insufficient funds
- Fixed check-in foreign key constraint error for `receptionist_id`
  - System gracefully handles invalid receptionist IDs by setting to NULL
- Fixed checked-in rooms not displaying in dashboard
  - Corrected JavaScript destructuring of `checkoutSummary` in room data
- Fixed room availability validation in `room-detail.html`
  - Prevents booking attempts for unavailable rooms
- Fixed TabError (inconsistent tabs/spaces) in `checkin_service.py`
- Fixed requirements.txt security vulnerabilities
  - Updated Flask to 3.1.2
  - Updated flask-cors to 6.0.0
  - Updated mysql-connector-python to 9.5.0
  - Updated python-dotenv to 1.2.1

### Security
- Updated dependencies to latest versions to address security vulnerabilities

## [0.3.0] - 2026-01-02

### Added
- Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) system with middleware decorators
  - `require_auth` - Requires user authentication
  - `require_admin` - Requires administrator role
  - `require_receptionist_or_admin` - Requires receptionist or administrator role
  - `require_role` - Custom role-based access
  - `optional_auth` - Optional authentication
- Admin access restrictions - Admins cannot access user booking pages
- User role-based redirects after login/registration
- Frontend authentication middleware with automatic header injection
- Admin panel access control and navigation restrictions

### Changed
- Updated all API routes with appropriate authentication/authorization decorators
- Frontend API calls now automatically include `X-User-Id` header
- Login/registration redirects users based on their role (admin → admin.html, user → dashboard.html)
- Navigation menus adapt based on user role

### Fixed
- Admin users can no longer access user-specific pages (dashboard, booking, my-bookings, payment)
- Proper error handling for 401 (Unauthorized) and 403 (Forbidden) responses
- Session management improvements

## [0.2.0] - 2025-12-31

### Added
- MySQL database integration replacing in-memory storage
  - Database configuration module (`db_config.py`) with environment variable support
  - Connection pooling and error handling
  - Migration from in-memory dictionaries to MySQL tables
- Environment variable configuration (`.env` file) for database credentials
- Database schema implementation with all tables:
  - users, staff, rooms, bookings, payments, services, coupons, checkins, checkouts, reports
- Repository layer refactored for MySQL:
  - All CRUD operations now use MySQL queries
  - Transaction management with rollback support
  - Proper data type conversions and null handling
- Database connection testing script

### Changed
- All repository classes migrated from in-memory storage to MySQL
- Data persistence across application restarts
- Improved error handling for database operations

### Security
- Database credentials moved to environment variables (`.env` file)
- Connection strings no longer hardcoded in source code

## [0.1.0] - 2025-12-06

### Added
- Initial project setup
- Project structure with layered architecture (Models, Views, Controllers, Services, Repositories)
- Flask backend API with RESTful endpoints
- Frontend UI with HTML, CSS, and JavaScript
- Basic authentication system (login/registration)
- Room management functionality
- Booking system
- Payment processing
- Service management
- Staff management
- Report generation
- README.md
- Changelog

### Added - Core Features
- User registration and login
- Room CRUD operations
- Booking creation and management
- Payment processing
- Service catalog
- Staff management
- Report generation
- Dashboard for users
- Admin panel for administrators

### Added - Frontend Pages
- Homepage (index.html)
- Login page (login.html)
- Registration page (register.html)
- Dashboard (dashboard.html)
- Booking page (booking.html)
- My Bookings (my-bookings.html)
- Admin Panel (admin.html)
- Payment page (payment.html)

### Added - Backend Architecture
- Models: User, Room, Booking, Payment, Service, Staff, Coupon, CheckIn, Report
- Controllers: UserController, RoomController, BookingController, PaymentController, etc.
- Services: Business logic layer for all entities
- Repositories: Data access layer (initially in-memory, later migrated to MySQL)
- Views: Response formatting layer
